{"Code calls Optional.get() without checking if the recovery-codes credential is present, which can throw NoSuchElementException at runtime if the credential is missing (e.g., feature disabled, user not configured, or storage/provider mismatch)": 0.9610310196876526, "Recovery codes are serialized as plaintext JSON and passed through user storage updateCredential, potentially storing raw recovery codes in external federated storage if the provider persists challengeResponse/credentialData as-is, increasing security risk if that store is compromised": 0.826641857624054, "Recovery codes are deserialized using raw List.class which is type-unsafe and may behave unexpectedly if the stored JSON isn't a List<String>": 0.8468983769416809, "getCredentials() logs and continues on deserialization failure instead of properly handling the error, which may hide test/provider regressions": 0.6089481711387634}